{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:5e10922bdbc32ec8","name":"Marker Missiles","source":{"id":"source:reference-5e10922bdbc32ec8","title":"Marker Missiles","revision":21873,"timestamp":"2024-08-27T17:24:52Z","sha256":"362aed13143f7636863a461ce5ce5739bee53fc5d71ab2e93490ca7c5ed0f143","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21873","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Marker%20Missiles&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-5e10922bdbc32ec8","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy at War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_at_War"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," successfully track targets by one of two methods. The most reliable way is to tag a target with an S-thread or other hyperspace tracking device, usually fired from the attacking fighter via a Marker Missile. While large ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," or freighters are easy to tag, fighters, shuttles, and other small craft are more difficult to hit. The second method is less reliable, as it depends on the fighter's own sensor array and navigational computer to analyze a fleeing ship's departure vector, engine output, and other data that might tip off its final destination. Often such calculations must be made with great speed, and the pilot must make some educated guesses and assumptions when presented with a list of possible destinations. Plotting hyperspace jumps at great speed is always a risky business.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["To trace a fleeing ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," with a tracking device attached, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," must make a DC 15 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check. To track a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," without a homing beacon, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," (or another ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"},") must have observed the ship's departure into hyperspace, and the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," must make a DC 25 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check (with a -2 penalty for each ",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"}," increment beyond Short in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"},"). In either case, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," adds the ship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," modifier to the roll. After this roll is made, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," must still make a standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Astrogate"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Astrogate"}," check to initiative the pursuit.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," missile weapons have 20 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"}," and DR 10 each; when a missile is reduced to 0 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},", its munitions explode dealing normal damage to any objects or characters within a 4-Square ",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst"}," radius.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"caption","children":["Marker Missile Ranges\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["RANGE BY CHARACTER SCALE\n"],"colspan":4},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["\n"],"rowspan":3},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["\n",{"tag":"p","children":["RANGE BY STARSHIP SCALE\n"]},"\n"],"colspan":4}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["POINT-BLANK\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SHORT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MEDIUM\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["LONG\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["POINT-BLANK\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SHORT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MEDIUM\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["LONG\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-450 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["451-900 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["901-2,250 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2,251-4,500 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-3 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["4-6 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["7-15 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["16-30 Squares\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
